[{"id":"VRCE-6-38-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":1,"english":"Seeing her husband, well the exceedingly powerful Laksmana, slain, Srta, afflicted with grief, burst into bitter lamentation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"136df1e38819967fed8629e5ed4c08daa3133e5406187d7c41a78630a7526dc7","compact":"5844ad7cf93bf079b71fb63b21cc039ed5e28e80d2b4e52b8cee81523ac1ab66","nasal":"5844ad7cf93bf079b71fb63b21cc039ed5e28e80d2b4e52b8cee81523ac1ab66"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":2,"english":"The soothsayers had said that I should have sons, and should never be a widow. But on Råma being slain, it sees now that those ones, possessed of knowledge, had spoken untruthfully. Those also, who having celebrated sacrifices and rites, had said that I should become the queen (of Rama), on Rāma being slain, seems today to have spoken a falsehood, although they are possessed of knowledge. They also asserted that I should be honoured of the wives of heroic kings as well as of my lord, but on Rāma being slain, they seem to have spoken a falsehood, although possessed of knowledge.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-2","DUTT-6-48-3","DUTT-6-48-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f3308d989d45e0241b53bba4499b7b7978a9aadb6fd2947e377b40011c24471","compact":"e9f9a5e3ca91740e260c3bf7157f26102da06405d82926e0da33407615895a5f","nasal":"e9f9a5e3ca91740e260c3bf7157f26102da06405d82926e0da33407615895a5f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":3,"english":"The soothsayers had said that I should have sons, and should never be a widow. But on Råma being slain, it sees now that those ones, possessed of knowledge, had spoken untruthfully. Those also, who having celebrated sacrifices and rites, had said that I should become the queen (of Rama), on Rāma being slain, seems today to have spoken a falsehood, although they are possessed of knowledge. They also asserted that I should be honoured of the wives of heroic kings as well as of my lord, but on Rāma being slain, they seem to have spoken a falsehood, although possessed of knowledge.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-2","DUTT-6-48-3","DUTT-6-48-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41ba00dc1f639c738dcbad91b097b15bfe54e6a923526372ecc10c9b8871f6e1","compact":"a1491b26e7e06b202bbc3515adeec93590a7ba13965648926b8ab58327d1583b","nasal":"a1491b26e7e06b202bbc3515adeec93590a7ba13965648926b8ab58327d1583b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":4,"english":"The soothsayers had said that I should have sons, and should never be a widow. But on Råma being slain, it sees now that those ones, possessed of knowledge, had spoken untruthfully. Those also, who having celebrated sacrifices and rites, had said that I should become the queen (of Rama), on Rāma being slain, seems today to have spoken a falsehood, although they are possessed of knowledge. They also asserted that I should be honoured of the wives of heroic kings as well as of my lord, but on Rāma being slain, they seem to have spoken a falsehood, although possessed of knowledge.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.547,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-2","DUTT-6-48-3","DUTT-6-48-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e67cb81d4d48b0f8e30dfd0705d5d83adab8d6372bf267a69584fd5a3a80dc9","compact":"7600371b4b00606abd2c637973836ecd08ec32573518609d5fd689bbe30e1134","nasal":"7600371b4b00606abd2c637973836ecd08ec32573518609d5fd689bbe30e1134"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":5,"english":"Those also, who having celebrated sacrifices and rites, had said that I should become the queen (of Rama), on Rāma being slain, seems today to have spoken a falsehood, although they are possessed of knowledge. They also asserted that I should be honoured of the wives of heroic kings as well as of my lord, but on Rāma being slain, they seem to have spoken a falsehood, although possessed of knowledge. Those twice-born ones that in any hearing had said auspicious words, on Rāma being slain, seem today to have spoken a falsehood although they were possessed of knowledge.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-3","DUTT-6-48-4","DUTT-6-48-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5574d22f181ce4c0412a93b58705b8b4a49cb341cb83de0b3da98ffff9a674b0","compact":"d23b33166d86df5538adb5ffc8ee6248832d90592ba8da3577676d696e8efd57","nasal":"306abe6090ab17d3bdd3211108067c23f8051aee8dd4376f67f0f6fd45ba9426"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":6,"english":"These lotus-marks on the feet, betokening to gentlewomen possessing them, that they are to be installed in the kingdom in company with their husbands-who are kings-are on me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.701,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c77e4bbc8af91dfe41b02b5ba2ff2c32c90edb00226cd758979bd5a5c279771f","compact":"41ab2e481082071b2307335dabb77afc6162409b63f7bc5943b070dfa0a00d57","nasal":"49e879ed6160facc5dd514d24b2a0ae17fd7784511ded12abcae656494f673bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":7,"english":"Those marks find I none on me by which women of rare fortune come by widowhood, but I find that in me these good tokens are nullified.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b3c44e2da704b9f2fa41c95faacc58f53219f2db13c3f518ea8af71f3458cd8","compact":"92859a8c11bb155a986400517af5ca3c04368badd6a86e717ac959a22606dfdf","nasal":"8fbefb5115fc8dfa8d1c1d6aa50374e165cf449b18b7fcf64c3efb0b69786715"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":8,"english":"Those marks that are pronounced infallible by those versed in such knowledge, on Rama being slain, are nullified in me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.642,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a762d6c57de1cbdcc16b7d427bc909630af8705fc912366cbed3acc2890cea97","compact":"276ff2f89b46a7ad8e09b533a4855e0db5260ea7ddaf86cbf25ecb84749186f2","nasal":"6c23b248fa3a7220b90c319f0fb39c94f1adea3e3e1d8484c3f18b72041ea518"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":9,"english":"My hairs are fine, equal, and blue; my eyebrows touch each other; my hips are devoid of down and round; and my teeth are close.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.476,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d22f9b307fe93c94cf721709d531bba990f61490d8b96af3520c6a064c5c05a1","compact":"08aea4370c9a59b33f1b7b56f7a620a58cd40e69fc664b89ade9dc9d8fd4ca4b","nasal":"04292ee4714be6ae7dbc2980844a8cf303c6669dcfeb884f854e6dadeae174a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":10,"english":"My temples, and eyes hands, feet, ankles, and thighs are equal. And my fingers are furnished with round nails, and are plump and even in the middle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.652,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"511dafceeae682378bb0a4923736587f2f6e3ed462318920df65fe0294be3581","compact":"860b7bbcc6f3df9ac594479309fbb8d23251712f403bbc976cabaf9b5fb3c9f5","nasal":"3485610a2c3524a8bf47393a4af8fce37233b7354acab02744263f3f88da230c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":11,"english":"And my breasts are close and firm and developed, and have their nipples sunk. And my navel is depressed, with high sides. And my chest is swelling.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.515,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd1d9c15e528e5fda383af66e5a512c1a4a87c19f59b8942cdf715aba927bc81","compact":"23c9528401a52c68fc0d53f81d7807347c3f6e95fa992e74d283de0a3ce8e285","nasal":"2283816b1098f732b76217b5385f60979627f48005a2656b43a941ba6cc76d8b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":12,"english":"My complexion is like the hue of gems, and my down soft. And they said that I was furnished with twelve auspicious signs.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e5df15b48ba7b94724be3c4e2dc1da4d1775ab15d26ed4caebec797d7cb6feb","compact":"2a73289bada5f5aaa0a951faa914648f35a7f1ad9693436663b0d666a41a357c","nasal":"3da46c5c3be0567fc411103e1aa1aa0ad7b9569b4d9a71c362afd27345e4bbb8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":13,"english":"And my hands in the middle parts of my fingers contain wheat-marks, and in the spaces between the fingers, have no uneven corners. And my feet also partake of the general complexion. And my laugh is a gentle smile. And those versed in marks of women knew that I was possessed of such marks.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c8ebf30e071c8ff05276e8cef624d6cba842056860daf53b948a042f81cad22","compact":"8b557a54af40ba30b6ee1bac2da415cd73e00080222c0c6eef52385e80a631e4","nasal":"d44ce5b4dfcafaf0eb1e2391ca318da42a08778fb7819d7e008d10beac1f6672"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":14,"english":"Those Brähmaņas skilled in telling fortune said that I should be installed in the kingdom along with my husband; but all that has been falsified.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.984,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da9b3cbd8acf35e8b6ba06c3e6e8833a190e59041242f9133ae4a9cc8370fe3a","compact":"0bcce989b80f89cc7d975fb36358d58d37a82980f02a94acba1e934e89cc6854","nasal":"817eb431325913450c7c27d618fd3936d1d615fe2ed62e4f71ccf17e0e38d846"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":15,"english":"Having purified Janasthana (of Raksasas), obtained tidings of me, and crossed the Ocean* incapable of being agitated, those brothers have been slain in the footprint of a cow! *The commentator assigns a metaphorical sense to ocean-but this is hardly necessary.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"684a73e785ccdb5a98faab6fb5e2f1e28028c10ba62bc172b18b3c14ef7d4a82","compact":"3349d6ae20c5aa4fc7a05c1be3b17f332d665c8364a21891707683125028340a","nasal":"3349d6ae20c5aa4fc7a05c1be3b17f332d665c8364a21891707683125028340a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":16,"english":"The descendants of Raghu had obtained Väruņa and Āgneya and Aindra and Vāyavya and Brahmasira weapons.* * And did they not remember this now? completes the sense.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0b7870bc8c4936ce573964cdbe7df6bad2d4b862b78dccba0e7819b6d7750132","compact":"78b18c76372df8166718a24b1728ea20588967d2126a64a518374563513f4ee4","nasal":"7f107537385afcb43a4429dca5b6464d68505e552d3f1bb9ccc240c769722464"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":17,"english":"Through illusion have those lords of me, who am forlorn. Rāma and Lakşmaņa, resembling Vasava himself in battle, been slain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.837,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42cac03105d6da1317e082eb6939c89430129e7c6503c089917a594fb9760c8d","compact":"a0baf965ae43eb944b220bf91a386b0d5cb1cab7bfbe966842e277af16c813fc","nasal":"a0baf965ae43eb944b220bf91a386b0d5cb1cab7bfbe966842e277af16c813fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":18,"english":"Coming in battle within ken of Raghava, a foe, even if he be endowed with the fleetness of thought, does not go back living.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9bc185ae9caf3519cb0923fb5db710bda9428d817d09706ea56e288a0a858aba","compact":"a0a3ac77ceaf5e94b64e8f3810e91495c4202425001c0c03cc7faf0d1e2de781","nasal":"a0a3ac77ceaf5e94b64e8f3810e91495c4202425001c0c03cc7faf0d1e2de781"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":19,"english":"There is nothing which is too hard for Time; and the Destroyer is incapable of being overcome; inasmuch as Rāma along with his brother Lakşmaņa has fallen in fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.938,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34b13b57d49c73fb6b695e59983f93117c51cb59b22bd617303f0d9d1e5baacd","compact":"bfb7324ce80ef3a3c69a92bc1d21516fce572e9f35b69f918fc0801a7a6bb84c","nasal":"1bff362ec2ec980dd2bbd1123473fd59a296a8ef84f60d69c3ec0049d77e354d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":20,"english":"I do not so much mourn Rāma or the mighty car-warrior-Laksmana-or, for that matter, self, as I do the wretched mother-in-law of mine. She ever think of the period of the promise. \"When shall I behold Sītā and Lakşmaņa with Rāghava?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.286,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6731c16283e3edf538fdd98d57090f3b8f5d0c3096ca5b4b29135d4e36cbd3d1","compact":"e3b0b81b3e02cbcc62816b4fd7215783f0603fcce368aba7a4166063e8ec0c53","nasal":"e3b0b81b3e02cbcc62816b4fd7215783f0603fcce368aba7a4166063e8ec0c53"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":21,"english":"I do not so much mourn Rāma or the mighty car-warrior-Laksmana-or, for that matter, self, as I do the wretched mother-in-law of mine. She ever think of the period of the promise. \"When shall I behold Sītā and Lakşmaņa with Rāghava?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04976b5e7b4b478438bfba78f4aab203c11baddac10bd4eafb97be1d35a3a190","compact":"3e3713e32d9ffcc0735fe41e7bea24b1cffbee79baf852c5f6e949379419f6b9","nasal":"56eeb0f61b5d19e86aa15a3b9a04337d5b02f4e3c25bf239cbf870d32f2fe394"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":22,"english":"As she was thus lamenting, the Rākṣasai, said, O exalted lady, do not weep thus, your lord live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65b1577169029249ef41c05613255f79af5151cfd959de1e2bc98180a9fc0067","compact":"ee2c853ae4e1fed6f632f9d1f4b3a290ed2f74203e008936ee86b32efa6f6bd4","nasal":"ee2c853ae4e1fed6f632f9d1f4b3a290ed2f74203e008936ee86b32efa6f6bd4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":23,"english":"O dignified one, I shall unfold to you potent and probable reasons why the brothers Rāma and Laksmana live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50e96d97bcf154a57dfd0d43fa5c34ce0cb66dd8ce0a8e71f1313fbc2fb728e2","compact":"2c70b29fa4c52625b0e97fa5e7cd14e1bea4f90c90feab9fdb841b66cd35fe38","nasal":"2630559ee216f7b7bb71881cf3fd05e15dbcbbc60bb73cbef6052b8979610e5a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":24,"english":"When their leader fall, the countenances of the warriors in battle are not overspread with passion, or display cheerfulness and vivacity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a30e40f15fcbc2db9ccad4fb080bf6389076984cd08232c3becad1ecb03bb7f","compact":"e9d6d18446b9f3f40fb3ee13d762e01f90cccf97fe0edbd4aee46dfd6e9d537b","nasal":"92ac39fc2b597cf1e99049028f4cc6eced54ea2c3ffdcac5085bdd5de864d515"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":25,"english":"O Vaidehi, if those had lost their lives, this celestial chariot, named Puspaka, would not have held you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de497e729587df549fb79b240e281405de58d60aaa59566e1bd0d5a24bd7f5b7","compact":"37f222e21c218a9ceba5973c5972493047c1f4bd049cd31d15c476f28a5e0a49","nasal":"9d71c2c44fd1657f9a43b6eca362e2264f2381a7eacef48171272192275a8449"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":26,"english":"An army that has its heroes and chiefs slainbecoming dispirited and drooping, range the field, like a vessel on water that has losi its helmsman. But, O lorm one, these troops, be trying neither agitation nor anxiety, are guarding the Kākutsthas, This I tell you of them out of affection.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.655,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b5bfa14678626b70e055b27e701567e8117944b3b33c22a4afdf43c41076c1f2","compact":"d8232d5485b758c549151ecc4e15a5879692efdbc4a338a3a2ade44f24fd3e71","nasal":"d8232d5485b758c549151ecc4e15a5879692efdbc4a338a3a2ade44f24fd3e71"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":27,"english":"An army that has its heroes and chiefs slainbecoming dispirited and drooping, range the field, like a vessel on water that has losi its helmsman. But, O lorm one, these troops, be trying neither agitation nor anxiety, are guarding the Kākutsthas, This I tell you of them out of affection.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.561,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"816467ad6f72fc4db9f491218ee884b206a06b9894ad49cdefd6882814576a4d","compact":"1c4ee8004d74aa1c37b7a606418853670b1554008e2f1fdfe9726dbbbd81895e","nasal":"9e2aa0a417f98fa00597d4f5dacaa24ef230f1b1a1e92997a3a595b4ffdb53ef"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":28,"english":"Do you, at this conclusion bringing in joy, take comfort; and behold the Kākutsthas unslain. This I tell you from affection.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fafa82eb7af651a88168a0299b0f1e929a69f072b7327eb4554ccc3057151373","compact":"cec5a543143ee7d8f77a87310dce08cbdb103c0d2133a8bba2a15be496322693","nasal":"cec5a543143ee7d8f77a87310dce08cbdb103c0d2133a8bba2a15be496322693"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":29,"english":"I never told you untruths heretofore; nor, O Mithila's daughter, will I tell them to you now. You by virtue of your character conducive to delight, have found an access into my heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.65,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c55ce5c2d0c738776a79dac4f3c2d41392e212be696113f363190cd0ba10d89","compact":"9460e8d78ffe92721c430857bbc9ff7f76ae8ba73ddb8e9191912eb37e0b5978","nasal":"9460e8d78ffe92721c430857bbc9ff7f76ae8ba73ddb8e9191912eb37e0b5978"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":30,"english":"These even the celestials and Asuras with Indra (at their head) are incompetent to quell. Seeing such sight, I speak to you as to their being alive.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.483,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e58a64446b5088abe160c8df4d0272dd0d3e01792dc13eb63ef32908c3e03e63","compact":"9156d0bcacefdec88f493745e3f2185f70f2a85a75f83c3f6ad386ee545da37d","nasal":"68a2060c4bd2855fd204d09d20ed3a6850c6f077164fe935971b45d456731197"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":31,"english":"And behold O Maithili, this mighty wonder! These are lying insensible with arrows; but of these Grace has not taken leave.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.313,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c4ee9bb9948950c2d06979453c59f325669f638c98438ac0c29f579a98ae6d9","compact":"1e93ace30c01e8a985da5fca413e63b609d9fa8093d1fd738574141e64198437","nasal":"1e93ace30c01e8a985da5fca413e63b609d9fa8093d1fd738574141e64198437"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":32,"english":"It generally happens that the faces of persons dead and gone, are unsightly to a degree. Therefore, O Janka's daughter, leave off grief and sorrow and stupor. For the sake of Rāma and Lakşmaņa you can not today put a period to your existence.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.766,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"93e7847bec38f86c765e3f330be7fa073f5cf0e6bf2aee8e7951a7ade1b22ca1","compact":"7ba8949df722f28e2d20da9dbb1a1fea579d2e4000b138f72f22585f416f68e2","nasal":"7ba8949df722f28e2d20da9dbb1a1fea579d2e4000b138f72f22585f416f68e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-38-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":38,"verse":33,"english":"It generally happens that the faces of persons dead and gone, are unsightly to a degree. Therefore, O Janka's daughter, leave off grief and sorrow and stupor. For the sake of Rāma and Lakşmaņa you can not today put a period to your existence.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-48-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6038033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2988e7d4